The `--n-cpu-moe` flag in llama.cpp controls how many MoE layers are offloaded to the CPU to conserve GPU memory during inference, enabling larger models to run on hardware with limited VRAM. However, performance is highly sensitive to NUMA topology—offloading across multiple CPU sockets can degrade speeds due to slow cross-node memory access, so optimal usage requires confining the model to a single NUMA node.
